### =====================================================================
### F12 — front-end bridge: device identity + pin → place
### =====================================================================

### B1. device A: anonymous identity → 201 {token, user}
# @name deviceA
POST {{base}}/auth/anonymous
Content-Type: application/json

{"display_name": "Telefon A"}

### B2. device B: another identity → 201
# @name deviceB
POST {{base}}/auth/anonymous
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### B3. device A: pin + name → new place → 201 created:true
# @name pin
POST {{base}}/places/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceA.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Rondo Mogilskie", "lat": 50.0656, "lon": 19.9585}

### B4. device B: same name 10 m away → the same place → 200 created:false
POST {{base}}/places/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceB.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "rondo mogilskie", "lat": 50.0657, "lon": 19.9585}

### B5. device A: report a broken elevator at the resolved place → 201
# @name pinReport
POST {{base}}/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceA.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"place_id": "{{pin.response.body.$.place.id}}", "element": "elevator", "current_state": "not_working",
 "severity": "critical", "nature": "temporary", "description": "Winda w przejściu nie działa."}

### B6. device B confirms → 200, state no, confidence 0.6
POST {{base}}/observations/{{pinReport.response.body.$.observation_ids[0]}}/votes
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceB.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"value": 1}

### B7. 400 — device A cannot confirm its own report
POST {{base}}/observations/{{pinReport.response.body.$.observation_ids[0]}}/votes
Authorization: Bearer {{deviceA.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"value": 1}
